Assembler-dialect boundary, not part of the two-assembler PASS above:
function-section-quoted.c emits GNU-as escaping for quote/backslash names.
The frozen Linux assembler (GCC-14/GNU as) produces exact .text.a\b and
.text.a"b names. Clang's integrated assembler retains the escape backslashes
in its names, despite both binaries returning 0. Thus direct use of LLVM's
assembler for those escaped names is NOT equivalent and is not counted PASS;
the kernel lane uses the fixed GNU assembler, not this alternate combination.

